<h2 id="qimqui-procedure" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">3. Procedure</h2>

<h3 id="qimqui-step1" style="color:#00695c;font-size:1.05em;font-weight:600;margin-top:0.85em">3.1 Scope lock (required)</h3>

1. Restate scope in **one short paragraph**: goal, touch areas (manifest, API, UI, tests), explicit non-goals.
2. Split into **numbered phases** with **`[ ]`** bullets (3–7 phases typical).
3. Add a **Quality bar** line per phase: tests to run (unit / integration / Vitest e2e as appropriate).
4. If **true product ambiguity** remains → numbered question list only; **stop** (same bar as **implref** step 1).

<h3 id="qimqui-step2" style="color:#00695c;font-size:1.05em;font-weight:600;margin-top:0.85em">3.2 Mini-plan file (when no plan path given)</h3>

Write **`cursor_gen/refactor_plans/new/REFACTOR_<SHORT_TOPIC>.md`** with:

- Title + one-line goal
- Numbered phases + `[ ]` checklists from step 3.1
- Quality bar subsection
- Line: **Execute with:** `qimqui` / **`aciub`** on this path

Skip lengthy prose, deferred tables, and evidence dumps unless the user asked for them.

If user **named an existing plan path**, use that file instead; normalize shape only if bullets are missing.

<h3 id="qimqui-step3" style="color:#00695c;font-size:1.05em;font-weight:600;margin-top:0.85em">3.3 Execute (required)</h3>

Immediately run the [Execution chain](#qimqui-chain):

1. Read and follow **`.cursor/rules/aciub-allow-continue-iterations-until-blocked.mdc`** (**`aciub`**) with the plan path.
2. **`aciub`** delegates impl to **`.cursor/rules/implref-resumimpl-refactor-plan-followthrough.mdc`** (**`implref`** / **`resumimpl`**).

Do **not** ask permission between phases. Do **not** stop after “plan written” — begin **`aciub`** in the same session.

---

<h2 id="qimqui-chain" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">4. Execution chain (classic)</h2>

**This section is the chain resolver for `qimqui`.** The TDD wrapper (**qimpltdd**) replaces every row below with its TDD path — see [TDD variant](#qimqui-tdd-pointer).

| Chain role | Keyword | Rule path |
|------------|---------|-----------|
| Optional full plan authoring (not used by default in qimqui) | **`onlyref`** | `.cursor/rules/onlyref-refactor-plan-author-only.mdc` |
| Continuous loop until blocked | **`aciub`** | `.cursor/rules/aciub-allow-continue-iterations-until-blocked.mdc` |
| Implement / resume plan phases | **`implref`** / **`resumimpl`** | `.cursor/rules/implref-resumimpl-refactor-plan-followthrough.mdc` |

**Default qimqui path:** mini-plan (or named plan) → **`aciub <plan.md>`** → **`implref`** inside **aciub**.

---

<h2 id="qimqui-stop" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">5. Stop conditions</h2>

Same closed list as **implref** §3.1d / **aciub** §8: true blocker, manual user action, scope complete, or session cut (§3.1e).

On session cut: plan in **`wip/`**; tell user to resume with **`qimqui`** or **`aciub`** / **`resumimpl`** on the **same plan path**.

---

<h2 id="qimqui-close" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">6. Closing summary</h2>

When stopping, use **implref** step 4 HTML table (phases, tests, war stories, plan path, blockers).

